.TH SPACEGL-DIAG 1 "2026-11-01" "SpaceGL @VERSION@" "SpaceGL Manual"
.SH NAME
spacegl-diag \- SpaceGL diagnostic scanner launcher script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spacegl-diag
.RB [ \-\-no\-banner ]
.RI [ PID ]
.RI [ "DIAG OPTIONS" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spacegl-diag
starts the real-time diagnostic,
.BR spacegl_diag (1),
on a running
.BR spacegl_server (1):
the one given by
.IR PID ,
or the only one running (found with
.BR pgrep (1);
with several the PID must be given). When a graphical display and
.BR xterm (1)
are available the diagnostic opens in a dedicated window (160x50,
monospace, green on black) that stays open if it exits with an error;
otherwise, or with
.BR SPACEGL_DIAG_TERMINAL=here ,
it runs in the current terminal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-banner
No banner and no screen clearing.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Usage.
.TP
.I PID
The process to watch: it must be a running
.BR spacegl_server .
.PP
Further arguments are passed to
.BR spacegl_diag .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SPACEGL_DIAG_TERMINAL
.B xterm
(default: a new xterm window when possible) or
.B here
(this terminal).
.TP
.B SPACEGL_BIN_DIR
Directory of the program to run. Without it the script looks in the
build tree next to itself, in its own directory (an installed
.IR /usr/bin ),
in
.I ./build
and
.I .
of the current directory, then in
.BR PATH .
.TP
.B SPACEGL_NO_BANNER
1: no banner and no screen clearing (like
.BR \-\-no\-banner ).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Set: no colours (they are also off when the output is not a terminal).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The diagnostic window was opened (or, in this terminal, the
diagnostic's own status).
.TP
.B 1
No spacegl_server running, several running without a PID, or a PID
that is not a spacegl_server.
.TP
.B 127
.B spacegl_diag
not found.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR spacegl_diag (1),
.BR spacegl_server (1),
.BR xterm (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Nicola Taibi
